4,31610,1124,1318,90,269,92,1124,31610,264,284,481,59,26888,90,21,532,256,1124,921,256,87149,17767,264,284,1124,26888,90,21,92,1124,8,1119,17767,668,488,293,284,481,17,15,15,20,1124,982,256,1124,9640,256,1124,26888,90,21,92,65,488,293,284,481,17,15,15,20,1124,6383,550,293,11520,26888,90,21,92,488,220,16,8,284,481,17,15,15,20,1124,6383,550,293,284,1124,37018,19999,17,15,15,20,15170,59,26888,90,21,92,488,220,16,532,256,1124,921,256,54525,551,279,46912,510,256,1124,9640,256,293,284,1124,37018,19999,17,15,15,20,11520,26888,90,21,92,481,220,16,9139,90,11520,26888,90,21,92,488,220,16,2376,59,26888,90,21,92,481,220,16,9139,284,1124,37018,19999,17,15,15,20,11520,26888,90,21,92,481,220,16,9139,90,21,481,220,16,92,284,1124,37018,19999,17,15,15,20,11520,26888,90,21,92,481,220,16,9139,90,20,92,284,481,19,15,16,11520,26888,90,21,92,481,220,16,340,256,1124,21675,522,37420,91339,29,151645,198,151644,872,198,2610,1231,312,18883,55856,279,3491,323,18130,279,6291,504,279,7167,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe function $f(x)$ satisfies\n\\[f(f(x)) = 6x - 2005\\]for all real numbers $x.$  There exists an integer $n$ such that $f(n) = 6n - 2005.$  Find $n.$\n\nPartial draft:\n<partial_draft>\nTo solve for \\( n \\) such that \\( f(n) = 6n - 2005 \\) given the functional equation \\( f(f(x)) = 6x - 2005 \\), we will proceed step by step.\n\n1. **Assume \\( f(n) = 6n - 2005 \\):**\n   \\[\n   f(f(n)) = f(6n - 2005)\n   \\]\n   According to the functional equation:\n   \\[\n   f(f(n)) = 6n - 2005\n   \\]\n   Therefore:\n   \\[\n   f(6n - 2005) = 6n - 2005\n   \\]\n\n2. **Analyze the fixed point:**\n   We have:\n   \\[\n   f(6n - 2005) = 6n - 2005\n   \\]\n   This suggests that \\( 6n - 2005 \\) is a fixed point of the function \\( f \\).\n\n3. **Check the form of \\( f(x) \\):**\n   Since \\( f(f(x)) = 6x - 2005 \\), we hypothesize that \\( f(x) \\) might be a linear function. Let:\n   \\[\n   f(x) = ax + b\n   \\]\n   Substitute \\( f(x) = ax + b \\) into the functional equation:\n   \\[\n   f(f(x)) = f(ax + b) = a(ax + b) + b = a^2x + ab + b\n   \\]\n   According to the given equation:\n   \\[\n   a^2x + ab + b = 6x - 2005\n   \\]\n   By comparing coefficients, we get:\n   \\[\n   a^2 = 6 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad ab + b = -2005\n   \\]\n\n4. **Solve for \\( a \\) and \\( b \\):**\n   From \\( a^2 = 6 \\), we have:\n   \\[\n   a = \\sqrt{6} \\quad \\text{or} \\quad a = -\\sqrt{6}\n   \\]\n   Substitute \\( a = \\sqrt{6} \\) into \\( ab + b = -2005 \\):\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{6}b + b = -2005 \\implies b(\\sqrt{6} + 1) = -2005 \\implies b = \\frac{-2005}{\\sqrt{6} + 1}\n   \\]\n   Rationalize the denominator:\n   \\[\n   b = \\frac{-2005(\\sqrt{6} - 1)}{(\\sqrt{6} + 1)(\\sqrt{6} - 1)} = \\frac{-2005(\\sqrt{6} - 1)}{6 - 1} = \\frac{-2005(\\sqrt{6} - 1)}{5} = -401(\\sqrt{6} - 1)\n   \\]\n\n\n</partial_draft>","role":"user"},{"content":"You may re-analyze the problem and rewrite the solution from the beginning.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"f0b70d84eaae9e397f8cc85330ddae93b69f7b380fc525715c83ca397063b5b5"},"seconds":76.3282458782196,"seed":922388159437968209,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we start by examining the given functional equation:\n\\[ f(f(x)) = 6x - 2005. \\]\nWe are also given that there exists an integer \\( n \\) such that \\( f(n) = 6n - 2005 \\). We need to find the value of \\( n \\).\n\nFirst, substitute \\( n \\) into the functional equation:\n\\[ f(f(n)) = 6n - 2005. \\]\nSince \\( f(n) = 6n - 2005 \\), we have:\n\\[ f(f(n)) = f(6n - 2005). \\]\nThus, the equation becomes:\n\\[ f(6n - 2005) = 6n - 2005. \\]\nThis means that \\( 6n - 2005 \\) is a fixed point of the function \\( f \\). Therefore, we have:\n\\[ f(6n - 2005) = 6n - 2005. \\]\n\nNext, let's consider the form of the function \\( f \\). Since \\( f(f(x)) = 6x - 2005 \\), we hypothesize that \\( f(x) \\) could be a linear function of the form \\( f(x) = ax + b \\). Substituting \\( f(x) = ax + b \\) into the functional equation, we get:\n\\[ f(f(x)) = f(ax + b) = a(ax + b) + b = a^2x + ab + b. \\]\nThis must equal \\( 6x - 2005 \\), so we have:\n\\[ a^2x + ab + b = 6x - 2005. \\]\nBy comparing coefficients, we get:\n\\[ a^2 = 6 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad ab + b = -2005. \\]\nFrom \\( a^2 = 6 \\), we have \\( a = \\sqrt{6} \\) or \\( a = -\\sqrt{6} \\).\n\nLet's consider the case \\( a = \\sqrt{6} \\). Then we have:\n\\[ ab + b = -2005 \\implies \\sqrt{6}b + b = -2005 \\implies b(\\sqrt{6} + 1) = -2005 \\implies b = \\frac{-2005}{\\sqrt{6} + 1}. \\]\nRationalizing the denominator, we get:\n\\[ b = \\frac{-2005(\\sqrt{6} - 1)}{(\\sqrt{6} + 1)(\\sqrt{6} - 1)} = \\frac{-2005(\\sqrt{6} - 1)}{6 - 1} = \\frac{-2005(\\sqrt{6} - 1)}{5} = -401(\\sqrt{6} - 1). \\]\nThis gives us the function:\n\\[ f(x) = \\sqrt{6}x - 401(\\sqrt{6} - 1). \\]\n\nNow, we need to find \\( n \\) such that \\( f(n) = 6n - 2005 \\). Substituting \\( f(x) \\) into this equation, we get:\n\\[ \\sqrt{6}n - 401(\\sqrt{6} - 1) = 6n - 2005. \\]\nRearranging terms, we have:\n\\[ \\sqrt{6}n - 6n = 401(\\sqrt{6} - 1) - 2005 \\implies n(\\sqrt{6} - 6) = 401\\sqrt{6} - 401 - 2005 \\implies n(\\sqrt{6} - 6) = 401\\sqrt{6} - 2406. \\]\nDividing both sides by \\( \\sqrt{6} - 6 \\), we get:\n\\[ n = \\frac{401\\sqrt{6} - 2406}{\\sqrt{6} - 6}. \\]\nRationalizing the denominator, we get:\n\\[ n = \\frac{(401\\sqrt{6} - 2406)(\\sqrt{6} + 6)}{(\\sqrt{6} - 6)(\\sqrt{6} + 6)} = \\frac{401 \\cdot 6 + 401 \\cdot 6\\sqrt{6} - 2406\\sqrt{6} - 2406 \\cdot 6}{6 - 36} = \\frac{2406 + 2406\\sqrt{6} - 2406\\sqrt{6} - 14436}{-30} = \\frac{2406 - 14436}{-30} = \\frac{-12030}{-30} = 401. \\]\nThus, the value of \\( n \\) is:\n\\[ \\boxed{401}. \\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{401}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To solve the problem, we start by examining the given functional equation:\n\\[ f(f(x)) = 6x - 2005. \\]\nWe are also given that there exists an integer \\( n \\) such that \\( f(n) = 6n - 2005 \\). We need to find the value of \\( n \\).\n\nFirst, substitute \\( n \\) into the functional equation:\n\\[ f(f(n)) = 6n - 2005. \\]\nSince \\( f(n) = 6n - 2005 \\), we have:\n\\[ f(f(n)) = f(6n - 2005). \\]\nThus, the equation becomes:\n\\[ f(6n - 2005) = 6n - 2005. \\]\nThis means that \\( 6n - 2005 \\) is a fixed point of the function \\( f \\). Therefore, we have:\n\\[ f(6n - 2005) = 6n - 2005. \\]\n\nNext, let's consider the form of the function \\( f \\). Since \\( f(f(x)) = 6x - 2005 \\), we hypothesize that \\( f(x) \\) could be a linear function of the form \\( f(x) = ax + b \\). Substituting \\( f(x) = ax + b \\) into the functional equation, we get:\n\\[ f(f(x)) = f(ax + b) = a(ax + b) + b = a^2x + ab + b. \\]\nThis must equal \\( 6x - 2005 \\), so we have:\n\\[ a^2x + ab + b = 6x - 2005. \\]\nBy comparing coefficients, we get:\n\\[ a^2 = 6 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad ab + b = -2005. \\]\nFrom \\( a^2 = 6 \\), we have \\( a = \\sqrt{6} \\) or \\( a = -\\sqrt{6} \\).\n\nLet's consider the case \\( a = \\sqrt{6} \\). Then we have:\n\\[ ab + b = -2005 \\implies \\sqrt{6}b + b = -2005 \\implies b(\\sqrt{6} + 1) = -2005 \\implies b = \\frac{-2005}{\\sqrt{6} + 1}. \\]\nRationalizing the denominator, we get:\n\\[ b = \\frac{-2005(\\sqrt{6} - 1)}{(\\sqrt{6} + 1)(\\sqrt{6} - 1)} = \\frac{-2005(\\sqrt{6} - 1)}{6 - 1} = \\frac{-2005(\\sqrt{6} - 1)}{5} = -401(\\sqrt{6} - 1). \\]\nThis gives us the function:\n\\[ f(x) = \\sqrt{6}x - 401(\\sqrt{6} - 1). \\]\n\nNow, we need to find \\( n \\) such that \\( f(n) = 6n - 2005 \\). Substituting \\( f(x) \\) into this equation, we get:\n\\[ \\sqrt{6}n - 401(\\sqrt{6} - 1) = 6n - 2005. \\]\nRearranging terms, we have:\n\\[ \\sqrt{6}n - 6n = 401(\\sqrt{6} - 1) - 2005 \\implies n(\\sqrt{6} - 6) = 401\\sqrt{6} - 401 - 2005 \\implies n(\\sqrt{6} - 6) = 401\\sqrt{6} - 2406. \\]\nDividing both sides by \\( \\sqrt{6} - 6 \\), we get:\n\\[ n = \\frac{401\\sqrt{6} - 2406}{\\sqrt{6} - 6}. \\]\nRationalizing the denominator, we get:\n\\[ n = \\frac{(401\\sqrt{6} - 2406)(\\sqrt{6} + 6)}{(\\sqrt{6} - 6)(\\sqrt{6} + 6)} = \\frac{401 \\cdot 6 + 401 \\cdot 6\\sqrt{6} - 2406\\sqrt{6} - 2406 \\cdot 6}{6 - 36} = \\frac{2406 + 2406\\sqrt{6} - 2406\\sqrt{6} - 14436}{-30} = \\frac{2406 - 14436}{-30} = \\frac{-12030}{-30} = 401. \\]\nThus, the value of \\( n \\) is:\n\\[ \\boxed{401}. \\]","id":"intermediate_algebra:569"}
